<h1>Instructions</h1>
<p>Before contributing, read these guidelines and the <a href="/about">about</a> page. Users are expected to be civil and factual, and to add only verifiable information — cases, news stories, and original documents — rather than personal views. Add as many supporting links as you like.</p>
<h2>Cases</h2>
<p>Most cases start as stubs. After many contributions they can become featured cases. You can also write and ask us to research a case that is not listed.</p>
<p>Creating and editing a case still happens on the Rails editor in this transition. The Hanami site reads the same rows after you save.</p>
<h2>Agencies</h2>
<p>Agencies are listed at <a href="/agencies">/agencies</a>. Creating or editing an agency is still a Rails write.</p>
